<p style="text-align: start;">
  Hello,
</p>

<% if @first_year %>
  <p style="text-align: start;">
    Thank you for being a part of GitHub for Startups!
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    We're reaching out <%= @days_to_expire == 5 ? "one last time " : "" %>because <b>your program expiration is coming up in <%= @days_to_expire %> days.</b>
  </p>

  <% case @days_to_expire %>
  <% when 30 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Want to continue on GitHub Enterprise? We're offering startups associated with <%= link_to("an approved GitHub for Startups partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %>
      a 50% discount on GitHub Enterprise for their second year in the program.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      GitHub for Startups Enterprise <%= link_to("features", pricing_url) %>:
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; 50K Action mins per month</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; User Management (SSO)</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; Organizational Controls (SOC)</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; ...and exclusive events, office hours, and webinars!</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>Interested in GitHub Advanced Security?</b> We're also inviting startups returning to the program and new to Advanced security
      a <b>50% discount</b> on GitHub Advanced Security!
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Code Scanning", DocsUrlConfig.url_for("code-security/about-code-scanning")) %> - Search for potential security vulnerabilities and coding errors in your code.</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Secret Scanning", "#{GitHub.help_url}/code-security/secret-scanning/about-secret-scanning") %> - Detect secrets (keys, tokens, etc.) that have been checked into private repos.</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Dependency Review", "#{GitHub.help_url}/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/about-dependency-review") %> - Show the full impact of changes to dependencies and vulnerable versions before you merge a pull request.</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If you're interested in the GitHub Advanced Security offer</b>: Please respond to this email and we'll connect you to someone for an evaluation!
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If you'd like to continue with only the GitHub for Startups Year 2 offer:</b> Please keep an eye out for a follow up email in 2 weeks with further
      instructions - until then, we recommend <%= link_to("reviewing the users in your Enterprise", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise-cloud@latest/admin/user-management/managing-users-in-your-enterprise/viewing-people-in-your-enterprise") %>
      and ensuring you have a payment method on file as you'll be charged for the number of licenses in your Enterprise ($10.50 each) immediately upon renewal.
    </p>
  <% when 14 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Want to continue on GitHub Enterprise? We're offering startups associated with <%= link_to("an approved GitHub for Startups partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %>
      a 50% discount on GitHub Enterprise for their second year in the program. We're also offering a <b>50% discount on GitHub Advanced Security</b> - let us know if you're interested in learning more!
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If you'd like to continue with the GitHub for Startups Year 2 Enterprise offer: </b>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>1. <%= link_to("Review the users in your Enterprise", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise-cloud@latest/admin/user-management/managing-users-in-your-enterprise/viewing-people-in-your-enterprise") %> and adjust the number of <u>licenses</u> in your Enterprise as you'll be charged $10.50 per license immediately upon renewal.</span><br>
      <span>2. Ensure you have a valid payment method on file</span><br>
      <span>3. <u>Respond to this email within a week</u> and specify which <%= link_to("GFS partner", "https://github.com/enterprise/startups/partners") %> you're affiliated with.</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      We'll apply the discount a few days before your program expiration date to ensure a seamless transition.
    </p>
  <% when 5 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Want to continue on GitHub Enterprise? We're offering startups associated with <%= link_to("an approved GitHub for Startups partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %>
      a 50% discount on GitHub Enterprise for their second year in the program.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If you'd like to continue with the GitHub for Startups Year 2 offer</b>:
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>1. <%= link_to("Review the users in your Enterprise", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise-cloud@latest/admin/user-management/managing-users-in-your-enterprise/viewing-people-in-your-enterprise") %> and adjust the number of <u>licenses</u> in your Enterprise as you'll be charged $10.50 per license immediately upon renewal.</span><br>
      <span>2. Ensure you have a valid payment method on file</span><br>
      <span>3. <u>Respond to this email ASAP</u> and specify which <%= link_to("GFS partner", "https://github.com/enterprise/startups/partners") %> you're affiliated with.</span><br>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    <b>If you are not looking to continue on GitHub Enterprise</b>: please ensure you <%= link_to("delete your Enterprise Account", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise-cloud@latest/admin/managing-your-enterprise-account/deleting-an-enterprise-account") %>
    before your program end date. Failure to do so will result in getting charged for GitHub Enterprise upon program expiration.
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    Thank you again for building with GitHub for Startups! Feel free to reach out to us in the <%= link_to("GitHub for Startup support portal", "#{GitHub.support_url}/contact?tags=hh-github-for-startups")%> if you have any questions.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p style="text-align: start;">
    We're reaching out because <b>your program graduation is coming up in <%= @days_to_expire %> days.</b>
    Thank you for having been a part of GitHub for Startups!
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    At this time, we're offering you a GitHub for Startups graduation discount redeemable within 30 days of program graduation.
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    <span>&#8226; Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise - 20% discount</span><br>
    <span>&#8226; Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise + Advanced Security - 25% discount</span><br>
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    <b>If you're interested in the above, please respond to this email at your earliest convenience.</b>
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    <b>If you are not looking to continue on GitHub Enterprise</b>: please ensure you <%= link_to("delete your Enterprise Account", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise-cloud@latest/admin/managing-your-enterprise-account/deleting-an-enterprise-account") %>
    before your program end date. Failure to do so will result in getting charged for GitHub Enterprise upon program expiration.
  </p>

  <p style="text-align: start;">
    Regards,
  </p>
<% end %>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  The GitHub for Startups Team
</p>

<p style="text-align: start; font-size: small">
  <b>Resources</b>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start; font-size: small">
  <span>&#8226; Use our <%= link_to("Copilot-powered support", "https://support.github.com/success/copilot") %> and <%= link_to("GitHub Docs", "https://docs.github.com/en") %> if you need more help</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("GitHub for Startups repository", "#{GitHub.help_url}/github/GitHub-for-Startups-HQ/tree/main") %>: information for templates and additional use cases</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("GitHub Marketplace", "#{GitHub.help_url}/marketplace?type=") %>: shortcuts the open source community is adding</span><br>
</p>
